@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# USDC Pay
+
+A small, production-shaped dApp with a single job: **connect a wallet and send
+USDC to someone on Ethereum mainnet.** The `/pay` page shows your USDC balance
+(what you can send) and your ETH balance (what pays for gas), each with USD
+context.
+
+USDC is the real Circle token on mainnet —
+[`0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48`](https://etherscan.io/token/0xA0b86991c6218b36c1d19D4a2e9Eb0cE3606eB48),
+**6 decimals**.
+
+## Stack
+
+- **Next.js 14** (App Router, TypeScript)
+- **wagmi v2 + viem v2** — typed contract reads/writes
+- **RainbowKit v2** — wallet connection, account/network UI, ENS + avatars
+- **TanStack Query** — caching and polling for onchain reads
+- **Chainlink ETH/USD feed** — onchain price for ETH USD context (no third-party price API)
+
+## Getting started
+
+```bash
+npm install
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then fill in the values
+npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000  → redirects to /pay
+```
+
+### Environment
+
+| Variable | Required | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAINNET_RPC_URL` | production | Dedicated authenticated mainnet RPC. Falls back to a public endpoint (dev only) and the UI warns when unset. |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID` | for WalletConnect wallets | Free id from [WalletConnect Cloud](https://cloud.walletconnect.com). |
+| `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` | production | Absolute base URL used for Open Graph / Twitter image tags. |
+
+## How it works
+
+- **A USDC transfer needs no approval.** `transfer(to, amount)` moves the
+  sender's own tokens, so the four-state flow is **Connect → Switch network →
+  Send** (no approve step). Wrong-network is checked before the send is allowed.
+- **The send button owns its full lifecycle:** disabled + "Confirm in your
+  wallet…" while the wallet prompt is open, "Sending USDC…" while the tx
+  confirms, then a success panel with an Etherscan link. It's released in a
+  `finally` block so a rejected transaction never locks it.
+- **Amounts** are parsed/formatted with `parseUnits`/`formatUnits` at 6
+  decimals; the input rejects >6 decimal places and amounts above your balance.
+- **Recipients** accept a `0x` address or an ENS name, with paste
+  normalization, validation, and live resolution before the send is enabled.
+- **Balances** poll every ~4s and refresh immediately after a confirmed send.
+
+## Project layout
+
+```
+app/
+  layout.tsx          # metadata (OG/Twitter/favicon), providers
+  providers.tsx       # wagmi + RainbowKit + React Query, theme-aware
+  globals.css         # semantic light/dark theme tokens
+  page.tsx            # redirects to /pay
+  pay/
+    page.tsx          # route + metadata
+    PayClient.tsx     # header (ConnectButton), balances, form
+    Balances.tsx      # USDC + ETH balances with USD context
+    PayForm.tsx       # recipient + amount + four-state action
+    AddressField.tsx  # validated recipient input with ENS
+    CopyButton.tsx
+    icons.tsx
+    pay.module.css
+hooks/useEthUsdPrice.ts
+lib/                  # constants, abi, wagmi config, formatting, error mapping
+```
+
+> Sends interact with the real mainnet USDC contract. Transfers are
+> irreversible — verify the recipient before confirming.
